Hi

On 3/15/07, Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org> wrote:
> Greg, could we please either
>
> a) start doing something about these reports or
> b) publish sufficient info to permit others to do something about these
>    reports or
> c) remove the printk?
>

Thanks Andrew for considering.

I eventually tried to add "pci=assign-busses" as it was suggested by
the initial console output but I still have some issues I think. For
example:

$ dmesg
[...]
PCI: Failed to allocate mem resource #6:20000@d0000000 for 0000:01:00.0
[...]

I join the corresponding dmesg.

Hope that helps.
-- 
Francis

